NOTICE — what the MIT licence covers and what it does not

The MIT licence above applies to the original work in this repository: the
skill instructions (SKILL.md), the checker and build scripts (scripts/,
tools/), the evaluation harness (evals/), the glossary, and this README.

It does NOT apply to content derived from ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical
English, Issue 9 (January 2025), which is the copyright of the Aerospace,
Security and Defence Industries Association of Europe (ASD) and is an EU
registered trade mark. That content is:

  scripts/dictionary.json
  references/approved-words.md
  references/non-approved-words.md
  references/writing-rules.md            (rule text and examples)
  references/technical-noun-categories.md (category lists and examples)

ASD's copyright notice permits reproduction only with the written authority
of an officer of ASD, or by the organisations listed in the standard's
"Special usage rights". VoltSafe obtained its copy of the standard from ASD
through the official request process and holds this material for its own
internal use. This repository is private for that reason. Do not publish,
fork publicly, or share these files outside VoltSafe. Anyone who needs the
standard itself can request it free of charge at
https://www.asd-ste100.org/STE_downloads.html.
